# EtAvatar Component (V2)

## Purpose & Scope

`EtAvatar` is a compositional avatar component for the eToro design system. It provides a flexible, accessible avatar with:

- **Multiple sizes**: small (24px), medium (36px), large (48px)
- **Multiple shapes**: square (rounded rectangle), circle (fully circular)
- **Compound component pattern**: `EtAvatar.Image`, `EtAvatar.Fallback`, `EtAvatar.Badge`, `EtAvatar.MarketOpen` subcomponents
- **Variant support**: default, instrument (with gradient overlay)
- **Group support**: `EtAvatar.Group` with overlap and glass container

**Does NOT handle:**

- Navigation logic (use with router/navigation handlers)
- Press interactions (wrap in Pressable if needed)
- Loading skeletons (use `EtSkeleton` separately)

## Entry Points & Contracts

### `EtAvatar` (main component)

```tsx
<EtAvatar
  size?: AvatarSize          // default: 'medium'
  shape?: AvatarShape        // default: 'square'
  variant?: AvatarVariant    // default: 'default'
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>
  testID?: string
  // ...other ViewProps
>
  {children}
</EtAvatar>
```

### `EtAvatar.Image`

```tsx
<EtAvatar.Image
  src: string              // required - image URL
  alt?: string             // accessibility label
  onLoad?: () => void
  onError?: () => void
  // ...other ImageProps
/>
```

### `EtAvatar.Fallback`

```tsx
<EtAvatar.Fallback
  delayMs?: number         // delay before showing
  // ...other ViewProps
>
  {children}               // string or ReactNode
</EtAvatar.Fallback>
```

### `EtAvatar.Badge`

```tsx
<EtAvatar.Badge
  position?: BadgePosition // default: 'bottomRight'
  // ...other ViewProps
>
  {children}
</EtAvatar.Badge>
```

### `EtAvatar.MarketOpen`

```tsx
<EtAvatar.MarketOpen
  position?: BadgePosition       // default: 'bottomRight'
  status?: AvatarMarketStatus    // default: 'open'
  // ...other ViewProps
/>
```

Renders a fixed-size dot at the given corner. Shape-aware positioning. No children.
- `status='open'` (default) — green dot (`statusPositive`)
- `status='closed'` — red dot (`statusNegative`)

Visibility is consumer-controlled: omit the subcomponent entirely to hide the dot.

### `EtAvatar.Group`

```tsx
<EtAvatar.Group
// ...ViewProps
>
  {children} // EtAvatar components
</EtAvatar.Group>
```

### `EtAvatar.GroupCount`

```tsx
<EtAvatar.GroupCount>{children} // string like "+3"</EtAvatar.GroupCount>
```

### Types

| Type            | Values                                                           |
| --------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `AvatarSize`    | `'small'` \| `'medium'` \| `'large'`                             |
| `AvatarShape`   | `'square'` \| `'circle'`                                         |
| `AvatarVariant` | `'default'` \| `'instrument'`                                    |
| `BadgePosition`      | `'topLeft'` \| `'topRight'` \| `'bottomLeft'` \| `'bottomRight'` |
| `AvatarMarketStatus` | `'open'` \| `'closed'`                                           |

## Usage Patterns

### Basic avatar with fallback

```tsx
<EtAvatar size="medium" shape="circle">
  <EtAvatar.Image src={user.avatarUrl} alt={user.name} />
  <EtAvatar.Fallback>JD</EtAvatar.Fallback>
</EtAvatar>
```

### Instrument/Asset avatar with overlay

```tsx
<EtAvatar size="medium" variant="instrument">
  <EtAvatar.Image src={stock.logo} alt={stock.symbol} />
</EtAvatar>
```

### Instrument with market-status dot

```tsx
// Green dot (market open — default status)
<EtAvatar size="medium" shape="square" variant="instrument">
  <EtAvatar.Image src={instrument.logoUrl} />
  <EtAvatar.MarketOpen position="bottomRight" />
</EtAvatar>

// Red dot (market closed)
<EtAvatar size="medium" shape="square" variant="instrument">
  <EtAvatar.Image src={instrument.logoUrl} />
  <EtAvatar.MarketOpen position="bottomRight" status="closed" />
</EtAvatar>
```

### Avatar with badge

```tsx
<EtAvatar size="large" shape="square">
  <EtAvatar.Image src={user.avatarUrl} />
  <EtAvatar.Fallback>JD</EtAvatar.Fallback>
  <EtAvatar.Badge position="bottomRight">
    <OnlineIndicator />
  </EtAvatar.Badge>
</EtAvatar>
```

### Avatar group

```tsx
<EtAvatar.Group>
  <EtAvatar size="small" shape="circle">
    <EtAvatar.Image src={user1.avatar} />
  </EtAvatar>
  <EtAvatar size="small" shape="circle">
    <EtAvatar.Image src={user2.avatar} />
  </EtAvatar>
  <EtAvatar size="small" shape="circle">
    <EtAvatar.Image src={user3.avatar} />
  </EtAvatar>
  <EtAvatar.GroupCount>+3</EtAvatar.GroupCount>
</EtAvatar.Group>
```

## Anti-patterns

### ❌ Using subcomponents outside EtAvatar

```tsx
// BAD - will throw runtime error
<EtAvatar.Image src="url" />
<EtAvatar.Fallback>JD</EtAvatar.Fallback>
```

**Fix:** Always wrap in `<EtAvatar>`.

### ❌ Using square shape in groups

```tsx
// BAD - groups should use circular avatars
<EtAvatar.Group>
  <EtAvatar shape="square">...</EtAvatar>
</EtAvatar.Group>
```

**Fix:** Use `shape="circle"` for avatars in groups.

### ❌ Forgetting fallback

```tsx
// BAD - no fallback if image fails
<EtAvatar>
  <EtAvatar.Image src={user.avatar} />
</EtAvatar>
```

**Fix:** Always provide a fallback for user avatars.

## Dependencies & Edges

### Internal Dependencies

- `useEtoroTheme` - provides theme colors for fallback styling
- `EtText` - underlying text component for fallback text
- `AvatarContext` - React context for passing state to subcomponents

### External Dependencies

- `expo-linear-gradient` - gradient overlay for instrument variant
- `react-native` - `Image`, `View`, `StyleSheet`

### Design System Integration

- Sizes follow Figma specs (24px, 36px, 48px)
- Border radius uses design tokens (`X1`, `X2`)
- Group container uses glass effect with 60px radius

## Patterns & Pitfalls

### Fallback visibility

Fallback only shows when:

1. Image hasn't loaded yet (unless `delayMs` is set)
2. Image failed to load (`imageError` is true)

### Group overlap

Group applies `-8px` margin to create overlap effect. The glass container has padding to compensate.

### Instrument variant

When `variant="instrument"`, a gradient overlay is applied on top of the image to match the design system for asset/instrument logos.

### SVG background color (automatic)

eToro instrument SVG URLs encode brand colors in the filename:
`…/market-avatars/{id}/{id}_{bgHex}_{fgHex}.svg` (e.g. `1001_F7F7F7_2C2C2C.svg`)

`EtAvatar.Image` automatically detects this pattern, parses the background hex, and applies it as the container `backgroundColor`. No extra props needed — passing an SVG `src` is sufficient. The color is cleared when the component unmounts or the `src` changes to a non-SVG URL.

## Design System Integration

V1 -> V2 mapping for `EtAvatar` slots:

| Subcomponent | Slot | V1 token | V2 token |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `Avatar.Fallback` | initials background | `bgNeutralGreyPrimary` | `cardDefault` |
| `Avatar.Fallback` | initials text color | `textSecondaryNeutral` | `carbon500` |
| `Avatar.GroupCount` | `+N` background | `bgNeutralGreyPrimary` | `cardDefault` |
| `Avatar.GroupCount` | `+N` text color | `textSecondaryNeutral` | `carbon500` |
| `Avatar.Group` | stack container background | `bgGlassPrimaryOverlay` | `cardDefault` |
| `Avatar.MarketOpen` | dot fill | `statusPositive` | `verdictPositive600` |
| `Avatar.MarketOpen` | dot border | `bgNeutralPrimary` | `backgroundBase` |
| `Avatar.Badge` | badge background | `carbonStatic900` | (already V2 — no change) |

`avatarOverlayTop` / `avatarOverlayBottom` (gradient stops on the instrument variant) remain RGBA literals defined inline in `core/styles/colors.ts` and are not theme tokens.

## Behavior deltas vs production

`Avatar.Group` previously used `bgGlassPrimaryOverlay`, whose dark-mode value is a 25% black wash (`neutralOpacity[950.25]`). The new `cardDefault` token resolves to a 4% white overlay in dark mode — visually slightly lighter rather than slightly darker than the surface beneath. This is an intentional, modest delta from production: the avatar group now reads as a low-opacity elevated chip in both themes, consistent with `EtPositionCard` and `EtAvatar.Fallback`. The pre-V2 token had a `// TODO: change to liquid glass` comment indicating it was already flagged as transitional.
